\b CRM System Project Migration to Next.js\b0\par
Seminar Documentation\par
\par
\b Project Overview\b0\par
This document describes the migration of an existing CRM system from a traditional Express and React architecture to a modern Next.js-based web application. The project keeps the existing business domain, including companies, clients, invoices, invoice series, and activity logging, while improving maintainability, security, and developer experience.\par
\par
\b 1. Analysis of Software Requirements\b0\par
The project was developed to satisfy the following seminar requirements:\par
1. Analysis of software requirements.\par
2. Designing the database associated with a process fulfilling security requirements.\par
3. Design of system classes.\par
4. Implementation of the software system.\par
5. System testing.\par
6. Writing the documentation.\par
\par
The original CRM application already provided the core business workflows, so the migration focused on preserving functionality while modernizing the technical stack. The main functional areas are authentication, company management, client management, invoice management, invoice series management, and audit logging.\par
\par
